  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Alice has a string SSS of length NNN, consisting of lowercase English letters. She wants to remove a lexicographically minimal subsequence†^{\\dagger}† TTT from SSS such that after removing TTT, the remaining characters of SSS cannot be rearranged to form a palindrome.\n\nYour task is to help Alice by printing the subsequence TTT that satisfies these conditions. If no such subsequence TTT exists, print −1-1−1.\n\n**Note:** The empty string is also considered a palindrome.The empty subsequence is lexicographically the smallest of all.\n\n†^{\\dagger}† A string TTT is called a **subsequence** of another string SSS if TTT can be derived from SSS by deleting zero or more characters without changing the order of the remaining characters.\n\nString XXX is lexicographically smaller than string YYY, if either of the following satisfies:\n\n\nXXX is a prefix of YYY and X≠YX \\neq YX=Y.\nThere exists an index iii such that Xi&lt;YiX_i \\lt Y_iXi​&lt;Yi​ and Xj=Yj,∀jX_j = Y_j, \\forall jXj​=Yj​,∀j such that 1≤j&lt;i1 \\leq j \\lt i1≤j&lt;i.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN - the length of string.\nThe next line contains string SSS.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case:\n\n\n\nIf a valid subsequence TTT exists, print the size of TTT on the first line.The subsequence TTT on the second line.\nIf no such subsequence TTT exists, print −1-1−1 in a single line.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "SSS consists of lowercase english alphabets only.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\nabc\n2\naa\n4\nbbaa",
        "output": "0\n-1\n2\nba",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: We will choose the empty subsequence, as we cannot rearrange given SSS to form a palindrome.\nTest case 222: No matter which subsequence you choose, it is still possible to rearrange SSS to form a palindrome.\nTest case 333: We will choose the subsequence bababa, and remove it from SSS:\n\nb‾baa‾→subsequence baba\\underline{b}ba \\underline{a}\\xrightarrow{\\text{subsequence } ba} ba b​baa​subsequence ba​ba, as we cannot rearrange bababa to form a palindrome."
